  "methodology": "Each scenario runs N times on a fresh, seeded mock World (the seed drives probabilistic faults such as 429 bursts, ghost writes and a lying API). An independent oracle reads the final World state (goal met, collateral diff against the seed snapshot, grounding against schools.json, safety, and report honesty) and never trusts the agent's self-report. Failed runs get one primary failure class from a rule-based taxonomy. pass^k is the tau-bench unbiased estimate C(c,k)/C(n,k) of k consecutive runs all passing. The FakeLLM scripted policy needs no LLM key, so it measures harness and connector reliability. The verifier-off column is the deliberately weakened \"before\" config whose report trusts the executor.",
